- `tools/` — the launcher (`lt.cmd` / `lt.sh` / `lt.py`).
- `PLUGIN-ISSUES.md` — the cumulative plugin defect ledger.

## 3. Running the tools

```text
tools/lt.cmd doctor                         # Windows
tools/lt.sh doctor                          # POSIX
tools/lt.cmd <group> --help                 # discover commands
tools/lt.cmd project tracked {{ project_rel }}         # does git track exactly the record?
tools/lt.cmd project scaffold {{ project_rel }} --refresh   # after a plugin upgrade
```

Record here the interpreter pin and any environment variable each machine needs. The
launcher finds the plugin on any host it is installed on (`LITTRANS_PLUGIN_ROOT` overrides);
on a fresh POSIX clone give `tools/lt.sh` its executable bit once. When several hosts share
this repository through a git remote: pull before writing, one host writes at a time, copy
the PDF to `source/` on each host, run `project tracked` before every commit.

## 4. Workflow

Probe → prepare → verify → translate (optionally transcribe assets) → audit → revise →
approve → render. Use `workflow next` / `workflow status` for the pipeline position; the
stage names and limits are listed in `docs/LITTRANS.md`.

